{"kind":"report","text":"Ready for independent review at exact clean head 6dd30b0c5519802f29bf0f7781a9d0f2765bfbbf on request/stale-qualifier-integration, artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e82a49acf99a0a931dfa712af4266c1c94f11ec9.\n\nWHAT CHANGED SINCE THE REVIEWED HEAD. Nothing in behaviour. The single must-fix was mergeability: c472d46883ab99cf4b45e46de98fdeb8c014ec35 had merge base 4db6d10568bbbef47e5e4fb98e4eefc15bc5ae72 with main and git merge-tree exited 1 on the committed UI embed. All conflicts were in internal/service/uidist: main deleted assets/index-DRHpEzzb.js while the candidate renamed it to assets/index-Bwnparbi.js, giving rename/delete and modify/delete, and internal/service/uidist/index.html conflicted on content. Main had moved on again from the 41c9fc062cd2cb785d372c9cec4ef694da1dba52 named in the verdict to dfa51178104ea5c2a5c91e81ac72e3f8697b1759, and the integration is against that.\n\nHOW THE EMBED WAS RESOLVED. Not by hand. Every Go, TypeScript and documentation source merged without conflict, preserving both the thread-railway UI and the stale-qualifier sources. The whole embed was then regenerated with make ui and committed as built. make ui-check rebuilds and fails on any difference; it passes at this head, so the committed embed is byte-identical to a fresh build.\n\nWHY THE BUNDLE HASH EQUALS MAIN'S. The regenerated bundle is assets/index-D9L7B-wU.js, byte-identical to the one already on main. That is not a missed rebuild. The two browser files the qualifier work touches, ui/src/components/SequencePane.tsx and the statementWeight export in ui/src/lib/store.ts, are imported only from ui/test, never from ui/src/App.tsx, so rollup drops them from the entry graph. Building main's sources alone into a separate directory produces the same assets/index-D9L7B-wU.js and the same assets/index--ynpQeC8.css, which is the independent check that this embed is a real build of these sources. Both files are still exercised by the UI suite, which imports them directly.\n\nGATES AT THIS EXACT HEAD, with git rev-parse HEAD re-read in the same command as each gate and unchanged throughout. git merge-tree --write-tree main 6dd30b0c5519802f29bf0f7781a9d0f2765bfbbf exits 0. make vet clean. make test: 15 packages ok, 0 failures. make race: 15 packages ok under the race detector. UI suite: 49 pass, 0 fail. npm run build succeeds and make ui-check reports no embed difference. git diff --check clean, gofmt -l reports nothing, and the worktree is clean.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL PROPERTIES RE-VERIFIED AT THIS HEAD, measured against the live log at depth 1664 with a gs built from this exact head. 346 commitments: 24 reported and stale, 55 satisfied and stale, 13 withdrawn and stale, 28 whose whole status is stale. codex measured 21, 53, 11 and 27 at depth 1538, so the shape is preserved and the log has simply grown. All 24 stale reported rows keep the status reported and keep waiting_on set to the requester who owes the ratification, and every one of them renders in the Actionable section, not in Needs attention. Needs attention holds only stale terminal rows and status-stale rows: satisfied (stale), withdrawn (stale) and stale. Settled clean rows are still left out. The totals line reads reported 80 (24 stale), satisfied 164 (55 stale), stale 28, withdrawn 19 (13 stale): parallel counts, and no (28 stale) beside stale because the word would only be repeated. No row anywhere renders stale (stale). The JSON still carries stale=true, on 120 commitments. The browser agrees: workItemState treats stale as attention without changing the lane, so a stale reported row stays in review.\n\nMUTATION PROOF, three mutations applied and reverted, head unchanged throughout. First, reinstating the removed short-circuit in foldState.projectCommitments, the case that set status stale with an empty waiting_on before reports were consulted: TestStaleCommitmentPreservesReportedTerminalState and TestStaleCommitmentKeepsItsWaitingParty/promise both go red. Second, a surgical mutation that sets status stale and clears waiting_on only after the qualifier is computed, so the satisfied assertion still passes and only the reported row breaks: TestStaleCommitmentPreservesReportedTerminalState fails at fold_test.go:321 with Status:stale WaitingOn: where reported and the requester were expected. That isolates exactly the property that a stale reported row keeps its status and its waiting lane. Third, dropping Stale: commitment.Stale from the bounded Commitment: TestStaleReportedKeepsItsStatusLaneAndQualifier fails at view_test.go:221 with Stale:false. Reverting each returned the package to green and the worktree to clean.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e82a49acf99a0a931dfa712af4266c1c94f11ec9","branch":"request/stale-qualifier-integration","head":"6dd30b0c5519802f29bf0f7781a9d0f2765bfbbf","merge_tree":"git merge-tree --write-tree main 6dd30b0c5519802f29bf0f7781a9d0f2765bfbbf exits 0 against main dfa51178104ea5c2a5c91e81ac72e3f8697b1759","status":"ready-for-review","tests":"vet clean; test 15/15 packages ok; race 15/15 ok; UI 49/49; npm run build and make ui-check byte-clean; git diff --check clean; 2 mutations proved red then restored green"}}